= Systems biology — Technical =

A dynamical systems-biology model can take the form <pre>dx/dt = f(x,u,θ)</pre>where x represents measured or latent biological states, u perturbations/inputs, and θ parameters. Identifiability, parameter uncertainty, boundary choice, measurement noise, validation and intervention experiments constrain interpretation.

== Modeling / evidence cautions ==
* systems biology ≠ network diagram
* systems biology ≠ systems science applied only metaphorically
* large biological dataset ≠ systems-level explanation

== References ==
* NIH/NIGMS systems-biology program definition: integration of experimental and computational approaches to biological interactions and dynamics.
* Hiroaki Kitano, “Systems Biology: A Brief Overview”, ''Science'' 295 (2002).
* systems-biology literature on quantitative, iterative experiment–model cycles.
